R1 fixes: all verified on disk (D1 pre-decision recorded, sign-off gate, D3 mechanics, coverage rule, D2, tracking table, wiring checks, naming map, D4, stream rule, WindowCap, sequential deps, keyless probe note, transport-generic mock guidance).

### New findings

**MAJOR-1 — phase-02's coverage rule is not implementable as written.** `TransferLookupOpts` carries `{FromBlock, ToBlock, Kinds, PageToken, PageSize, HeadBlock}` — the adapter cannot see the request budget or `maxPages`, so "within the page/upstream budget" is unimplementable. Worse, under newest-first upstream there is **no honest emit-able "contiguous prefix"**: the coverage model books `streamMaxBlock−1` as contiguous-from-`fetchFrom` (service.go:385–388), so emitting the scanned high-side range `[stopBlock..fetchTo]` ascending over-claims the unfetched hole `[fetchFrom..stopBlock−1]` — the exact bug the rule exists to kill. The only honest emissions are ∅ (incomplete) or the fully-covered window — and rows scanned in earlier `LookupTransfers` calls must be carried across calls to emit at scan end, but the plan never says where (fat `NextPageToken`, adapter-side cache, or single-call drain). Each choice has a distinct failure mode: single-call drain is pool-blind inside the step (`charge()` tolerates overshoot but the pool can't stop a 500-page drain — request-global budget becomes advisory), fat token serializes MBs of rows, adapter cache is stateful-but-unpinned. Fix: pin the drain/buffer model + an internal per-call upstream-call bound (new config knob or `TransferLookupOpts.MaxUpstreamCalls`), and restate the emit rule as "emit zero rows until the window is fully covered."

**MINOR-1** — roadmap `Depends` unsynced (above). Executors reading the table see 11 parallel-safe phases touching the same `config.go`/`main.go`/`.env.example`/migration-number space.

**MINOR-2** — phase-12 D3 lists "none → null/unknown" as an all-disabled `source_id` option (phase-12:73–74), but under the chosen D1(a) re-key `source_id` is a PK column → NOT NULL. Same ripple: today's NULL-`source_id` writes (`srcID` invalid when adapter nil/unresolved → `writeDisabled`/`UpsertWalletIndexState` insert NULL, service.go:441–493) violate the new PK; `GetWalletIndexState :one` (net,wallet) returns N rows post-rekey; `ON CONFLICT (network_id, wallet_id)` targets in both MarkWalletIndexing and UpsertWalletIndexState need the 3-col key; and "which source's row serves the response" is undefined. The design doc is the right venue — but the plan should enumerate these as required answers so the sign-off gate can't pass with them open.

**MINOR-3** — phase-05 overview says "keep stream semantics per direction" (line 12), contradicting its own "never fake per-direction on a unified-list upstream" (line 31). If Moralis' wallet endpoints are unified/kind-split, this instructs the forbidden fabrication — partition by the endpoints' real axes (native vs token endpoint).

**MINOR-4** — phase-12's never-failover list omits `internal` (phase-12:96–98). Of 10 `ErrKind`s, 5 are failover-listed and only 4 + empty-page are never-listed; `internal` hangs in neither. The "ONLY on" framing technically covers it, but the explicit complement list is the cross-check and should be closed.

**MINOR-5** — tier-2 STEP 0 handles probe-FAILED → NOT-VIABLE but is silent on probe-BLOCKED (no key). Bitquery/oklink/tokenview/chainbase need keys: an implementer without them can't tell whether to code-unverified (per plan.md's merge-unverified policy) or write NOT-VIABLE — which would be a *false* claim since untested ≠ proven non-viable. One clause: probe-BLOCKED ≠ NOT-VIABLE.

**MINOR-6** — cross-adapter `transfer_index` divergence: stream partitioning differences yield different occurrence counts `n` for identical logical transfers (e.g., W→W seen once-per-direction vs twice-in-unified-list → `counts[gk][stream]` max differs, identity.go:130,175–181). Under option (a) there's no reset, so rows a new source doesn't reproduce persist orphaned in `transactions`. Acceptable as chosen semantics, but belongs on the design-doc agenda.

### Verdict

All R1 fixes and 7/8 R3 fixes verified on disk. One MAJOR spec gap remains in phase-02 (the newest-first drain cannot be bounded or buffered as specified), plus six MINORs — all small-text fixes. **CHANGES_REQUESTED.**

